From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:41:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Read and set the run loop timer's tolerance only where
 iOS 7 has it

CFRunLoopTimerGetTolerance and CFRunLoopTimerSetTolerance are iOS 7 and
macOS 10.9 API. With availability checking on, the module does not
compile for an iOS 6 deployment target without a guard, and without
availability checking the calls are weak imports that are NULL on iOS 6
and crash on the first timer. Behind #available, a timer on an earlier
release has no tolerance: reading it gives zero, and setting it does
nothing.
---
 Sources/OpenCombineFoundation/Helpers/Portability.swift | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Sources/OpenCombineFoundation/Helpers/Portability.swift b/Sources/OpenCombineFoundation/Helpers/Portability.swift
index 3d778f6..06cd4db 100644
--- a/Sources/OpenCombineFoundation/Helpers/Portability.swift
+++ b/Sources/OpenCombineFoundation/Helpers/Portability.swift
@@ -74,14 +74,19 @@ internal struct Timer {
     internal var tolerance: TimeInterval {
         get {
 #if canImport(Darwin)
-            return CFRunLoopTimerGetTolerance(underlyingTimer)
+            if #available(iOS 7.0, macOS 10.9, *) {
+                return CFRunLoopTimerGetTolerance(underlyingTimer)
+            }
+            return 0
 #else
             return underlyingTimer.tolerance
 #endif
         }
         nonmutating set {
 #if canImport(Darwin)
-            CFRunLoopTimerSetTolerance(underlyingTimer, newValue)
+            if #available(iOS 7.0, macOS 10.9, *) {
+                CFRunLoopTimerSetTolerance(underlyingTimer, newValue)
+            }
 #else
             underlyingTimer.tolerance = newValue
 #endif
